{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MolecularConstruction.IcePaulingResidual","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MolecularConstruction.IcePaulingResidual","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Choose.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.pauling_multiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.pauling_multiplicity","kind":"theorem","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/ice-pauling-residual.lean#L32-L38","doc":"**Pauling per-molecule multiplicity.** `C(4,2)·(1/2)² = 3/2`: the six\nH-orientations, each of the two shared bonds holding exactly one H with the\nindependent-estimate probability `1/2`. The molar residual entropy is then\n`S = R·ln(3/2)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:ice-pauling-residual","label":"prop:ice-pauling-residual","md":"quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/ice-pauling-residual.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Molecular.ice_orientations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Molecular.ice_orientations","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/ice-pauling-residual.lean#L28-L30","doc":"Number of ways a water assigns its two donated H's among its four\nhydrogen bonds: `C(4,2) = 6`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}